# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data — never commit audio or the dataset. (CLAUDE.md, rule 2)
# The ASVspoof LA set is ~8 GB extracted. Once a .flac is in git history it
# stays in every clone forever, so these rules matter more than they look.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/
*.flac
*.wav
*.zip

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Working output — regenerated by scripts, so it is not source.
# verify.py and inspect.py write here. What matters gets copied into
# phases/phase-N/artifacts/ at phase close, and that folder IS committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/
checkpoints/
*.pt
*.npy

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python environment and caches
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Committed on purpose.
# figures/*.png is not matched by anything above, so it is already tracked.
# But *.npy and *.pt WOULD match files copied into a phase artifacts folder,
# so re-include that tree explicitly.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!phases/**/artifacts/**
